<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices rise on poor supply.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices rise on poor supply.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices rose in dull trade on Wednesday on poor supply, traders said.</p>
<p>They said prices rose 50 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on poor arrivals. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained weak on heavy selling, traders said. Soyoil solvent fell 100 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined was down 300 rupees per tonne in thin trade and an easy undertone, they said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were weak as export demand was poor, traders said. Soymeal yellow was $300 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $115 per tonne in export and was 3,900-3,950 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
<p>Traders said business volume was dull and the undertone easy.</p>
